  "summary": "A distinctive woodcarving tradition of the Asmat people, known for dramatic poles, shields, and ancestor figures with dynamic compositions and surface relief.",
  "description": "Ascarvings feature bold, rhythmic patterns of intertwined figures, animals, and abstract motifs carved in low and high relief, creating a sense of movement and energy. These works serve ritual purposes in warfare, headhunting ceremonies, and ancestor veneration, with designs that reflect the Asmat cosmology and relationship with the natural world.",
